# Line endings are LF everywhere, including on Windows checkouts.
#
# This is not a style preference. Many tests in this repo assert on source as
# TEXT, and some of those patterns span a line break. With a CRLF working copy
# a pattern written with \n matches nothing, so the assertion passes
# vacuously on Windows and only means something on CI — which is how
# tests/ghost-rise.test.ts came to fail every CI run from 19 Nov while every
# local run reported green, and how five pull requests were merged onto a red
# main without anybody noticing.
#
# Green locally and red in CI is the worst way round: the instinct is to
# distrust the local change. The same hazard was recorded for Node versions in
# Phase 6; this is the second instance, and the fix for both is to make the
# two environments the same rather than to remember the difference.
* text=auto eol=lf
